{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132914,"nonce":"f8eMSEUPHQJxONOGCzcCZImPaH8=","message":"AMENDMENT from the learning-helper/curriculum audit — orchestrator, session 4.\n\n**The emergency posture never closes its loop.** This spec's text says \"verify\nSeekAndKill engagement, only then intervene (draft) by exception\" — and never\nundrafts. That is a real procedural hole, not playbook colour: the scripted\ntutorial has a dedicated `UndraftAll` instruction, and the `Drafting` concept\ncarries its own warning — *\"don't leave colonists Drafted forever - they'll\nstarve and become unhappy\"*. A drafted colonist does not eat, sleep or work. On\na ten-day unattended run, forgetting to undraft after one raid is a slow-motion\ncolony wipe that no alert names as such.\n\nThe loop needs an explicit exit condition and an undraft step, and 4.3 should be\nable to demonstrate it.\n\n**Two assumptions in this spec's text that the audits touched:**\n- `rwa status` at session start and `rwa watch` reporting status are both\n  satisfied as built (1.4 closed this session, verified live).\n- **Do not use `status.json`'s `activeOp` to watch a short command in flight.**\n  `PublishSnapshot()` runs BEFORE `DrainCommands()` in the same frame, and\n  `activeOp` is set and cleared inside that drain — so it can only ever read\n  `null` or `advance:\u003cid\u003e`. Found by 1.4's worker; confirmed.\n- The `until:` matcher set is `{ticks|letter|threat|alert|event}` and every one\n  is a journal tap over discrete events. There is no `condition` matcher — see\n  DESIGN's corrected Time model and the new issue 1.6 (fc287ba). Write the\n  play-loop's guards against what exists.\n- New issue 1.7 (8555381): an advance can currently tick underneath a\n  force-pausing modal, after which every timing-out letter silently expires.\n  Until that lands, a long unattended loop is not sound.","files":null}]}